  "_notes": [
    "⚠ THE COMMIT LEG IS BROKEN — issue 858, found by this capture. The confirming retry reuses the requestId as §0 law 3 requires; the ask's own claim/release advanced the engine version past the ledger's reservation, so the retry resolves as FinishSidecarWrite ('the mutation landed'), marks itself applied and never calls the engine. `confirmAttempt` records that no-op — replayed:true over an empty basket — rather than pretending the mechanism works.",
    "⚠ THE ONLY STUBBED PORT IN THIS SUITE: ICallCenterAtpSource is armed with a known availability, because ATP is a remote StockV2 hop and no stock service is reachable from the capture environment. Everything else here — the digest, the single-use token, the requestId ledger, the envelope, the state — is the live server's.",
    "ATP is a SOFT gate (§5.2): the confirm ALWAYS succeeds, it is never a block. A degraded stock read (null) produces NO confirmation step at all rather than a shortfall against zero (287).",
    "The SAME requestId rides both halves (§0 law 3) — one user action, one id, including the retry that carries the confirmToken.",
    "The ask returns the UNCHANGED state at 200. A client that treated pendingConfirmation as an error would render a routine question as a failure."
  ]
